Fix the compiler warnings of libqtcurve-utils, Qt, GTK 2 and the tests

GCC 16.2.1 and Clang 22.1.8 report 34 warning sites outside the deprecated
declaration family, which stays. Each compiler runs with -Wall -Wextra, and
again with -O2 and -Wp,-D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3. The fortified pair arms the
warn_unused_result attribute of glibc and the format overflow check, and
gives 11 of them. The code deletes each variable and each parameter name
that nothing reads, and casts each count to int.

A void cast silences the open call of the Qt 6 configuration code. It does
not stop GCC for a glibc call. The fork callback and the icon map command
negate the result and cast it to void. The vformat function of libqtcurve-
utils returns a null pointer when vasprintf fails.

The test code keeps the result of the other read, write and asprintf calls
and asserts it. The array compare of test-oneof converts both operands to
pointers with a unary plus. A content compare stops the test, because both
strings hold the same text. The two test buffers move from the stack to the
heap and keep their size. The last assertion of test-process compares and no
longer assigns, so it tests the number the child process sent.

The GTK 2 engine sizes the slider resource buffer from snprintf. A probe
over the 324 combinations of width, style and glow gives the same string.

The log tables lose their array designators and keep the order of LogLevel.
Six explicit instantiations follow their own specialization and add nothing.
nm -D --defined-only gives the same 692 exported symbols of libqtcurve-utils
before and after. The compare object of oneOf copies the string into a local
pointer before the null test.

A Qt 6 root gives the same golden report as the parent commit, byte for
byte. ctest passes twelve of the thirteen tests before and after.

The change sits on the branch work/build-warnings of the local tree. The
fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !14 on system/qtcurve holds
that branch as the source.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

